/* The matrix content of 'zero eigenvalue' for Variant U.  J_U's 9th row is the
 * gradient of F9_U with respect to the 9 states (id,iq,vcd,vcq,igd,igq,eta,th,dw).
 * Variant U has F9_U = 0 identically, so EVERY partial is 0:
 *   dF9_U/d(id)=...=dF9_U/d(dw)=0.
 * Therefore e9^T J_U = (0,...,0), i.e. for an arbitrary state-direction vector
 * x = (x1..x9), the row acts as  sum_k (dF9_U/dx_k) * x_k = 0.  This is exactly
 * 'e9 is a left eigenvector of J_U for eigenvalue 0' (e9^T J_U = 0 = 0 * e9^T).
 * We encode the 9 partials g1..g9 (each provably 0 since F9_U=0) and prove the row
 * annihilates every direction. */
Problem
  \forall g1 \forall g2 \forall g3 \forall g4 \forall g5 \forall g6 \forall g7 \forall g8 \forall g9
  \forall x1 \forall x2 \forall x3 \forall x4 \forall x5 \forall x6 \forall x7 \forall x8 \forall x9
  ( ( g1=0 & g2=0 & g3=0 & g4=0 & g5=0 & g6=0 & g7=0 & g8=0 & g9=0 )
    ->
    g1*x1+g2*x2+g3*x3+g4*x4+g5*x5+g6*x6+g7*x7+g8*x8+g9*x9 = 0 )
End.
Tactic "zero row annihilates all directions by QE"
  QE
End.
